## Producer per-request timeout retry continuation — 2026-10-14T11:18:55Z

- Compared pinned Java `DefaultMQProducerImpl.sendDefaultImpl` and
  `sendKernelImpl` with Rust `send_default_until`. Java catches a local
  request-scoped `RemotingTooMuchRequestException` and proceeds to the next
  sync retry while the overall send budget remains. Rust returned a local
  `ProducerError::Timeout` without retrying.
- Added the invoked Java `perRequestTimeoutRetry` fixture. It configures
  request cap 0 with one retry, uses a 5 ms send hook to force the local
  timeout before transport on the first attempt, and records two before/after
  hook invocations. It also records that Java accepts setter inputs `-2`,
  `-1`, `0`, `125`, and `6000`. Fixture SHA-256:
  `c303c79a59a2bc7220aae6c488d9dc6cfda18d28590aa3f4d8a50af55e8c4dc8`.
- The new Rust regression failed before the fix: 2 hook calls versus Java's 4.
  Rust now retries local timeouts only for sync attempts with a stricter
  request deadline, a later configured attempt, and remaining total budget.
  Boundary tests cover disabled sentinels, zero and positive caps, total
  deadline clamping, and Future/Oneway/final-attempt exclusions.
- PASS: producer crate tests (134 unit tests and all integration/doc targets);
  strict producer all-target/all-feature Clippy; pinned Maven verify (37
  scenarios, fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); comparator self-test;
  37-scenario manifest validation; fmt and diff checks.
- Commits: `8ae5183a` Java oracle/fixture, `0a7e7ce2` Rust fix and regression,
  `3c17e8de` compatibility documentation. The log commit follows separately.
- This closes the per-request timeout/retry slice only. Full P18-V01
